<tr>
  <td class="pin-col name font-medium text-slate-900"><%= user.display_name %></td>
  <td><%= user.email %></td>
  <td><%= user.org_role %></td>
  <td class="date"><%= user.current_sign_in_at&.strftime("%Y/%m/%d") %></td>
  <td><%= user.invitation_status %></td>
  <td class="whitespace-nowrap"><%= reinvite_user_link(user) %></td>
  <td class="cell-actions">
    <%#
      Which actions exist depends on the user's role and on whether they are you, so inline the
      column showed two controls, then one, then nothing, row after row. That is the case
      design.md now says to collapse whatever the count -- the trigger is 28px on every row.

      A row with nothing available still gets the menu, holding the reason: you cannot act on your
      own membership. Better than an empty cell, which says nothing at all.
    %>
    <%
      is_admin = user.has_cached_role?(Role::ORG_ADMIN, current_organization)
      row_items = []
      unless is_admin
        row_items << {label: "Promote to admin", path: promote_to_org_admin_organization_path(user_id: user.id),
                      icon: "bi-arrow-up-circle", method: :post,
                      confirm: "This will promote the user to admin status. Are you sure that you want to submit this?"}
        row_items << {label: "Remove user", path: remove_user_organization_path(user_id: user.id),
                      icon: "bi-person-dash", method: :post, tone: :danger,
                      confirm: "This will revoke the user's organization permissions. Are you sure that you want to submit this?"}
      end
      if current_user.is_admin?(current_organization) && is_admin && user.id != current_user.id
        row_items << {label: "Demote to user",
                      path: demote_to_user_organization_path(user_id: user.id, organization_id: current_organization.id),
                      icon: "bi-arrow-down-circle", method: :post,
                      confirm: "This will demote the admin to user status. Are you sure that you want to submit this?"}
      end
      # Nothing to offer on your own row, and nothing the server could usefully be asked -- so
      # this one stays a disabled item. It is the exception design.md names: an action that is
      # unavailable because of *who you are* rather than because of the record's state, where
      # there is no attempt to make and therefore nothing for a flash to answer.
      if row_items.empty?
        row_items << {label: "Change this account", path: "#", icon: "bi-person-gear", disabled: true,
                      reason: "You cannot change your own membership"}
      end
    %>
    <%# `preferred_name`, not `display_name`: the latter falls back to the literal string "Name Not
        Provided", so every user who has not filled in a name produces the *same* accessible name.
        Measured on /organization: **four triggers all called "More actions for Name Not
        Provided"**, which a screen reader user cannot tell apart, and which the confirm audit could
        not reach either. `preferred_name` falls back to the email, which every user has and no two
        share. The visible cell still reads "Name Not Provided" -- that is a fine thing to *show*
        and a useless thing to be *called*. %>
    <%= render "shared/essentials/row_actions", label: user.preferred_name, items: row_items %>
  </td>
</tr>
